-- title:
--   W(mathbb F_{p²}) as mathbb Zₚ[ω] with σω = t-ω
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a natural number that is prime (as a `Fact` instance), and let $t, n$ be integers such that the quadratic $x^2 - tx + n$ has no root in $\mathbb Z/p$, i.e. $x^2 - \bar t x + \bar n \neq 0$ for every $x \in \mathbb Z/p$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a ring homomorphism $\iota : \mathbb Z_p \to W(\mathbb F_{p^2})$, where $W(\mathbb F_{p^2})$ is the ring of Witt vectors `WittVector p (GaloisField p 2)` over the Galois field of order $p^2$, and of an element $\omega \in W(\mathbb F_{p^2})$, such that: (i) the Witt-vector Frobenius fixes the image of $\iota$, i.e. $\mathrm{frob}(\iota c) = \iota c$ for all $c \in \mathbb Z_p$; (ii) $\omega^2 = t\omega - n$, the integers $t,n$ being taken in $W(\mathbb F_{p^2})$ via the canonical ring map; (iii) $\mathrm{frob}(\omega) = t - \omega$; (iv) $1, \omega$ are $\mathbb Z_p$-independent in the strong sense that $\iota c + (\iota d)\,\omega = 0$ forces $c = d = 0$; and (v) for every natural number $k$ and every $x \in W(\mathbb F_{p^2})$ there are rational integers $c, d$ with $x - (c + d\omega)$ in the ideal generated by $p^k$. Thus (v) expresses $p$-adic density of $\mathbb Z + \mathbb Z\omega$, with integral rather than $p$-adic coefficients.
--
--   This is the explicit description of the ring of integers $\mathbb Z_{p^2}$ of the unramified quadratic extension of $\mathbb Q_p$ as $\mathbb Z_p[\omega]$, realised on Witt vectors over $\mathbb F_{p^2}$, with the Frobenius acting by $\omega \mapsto t - \omega$ on a root of a prescribed quadratic that is irreducible modulo $p$. It is used to coordinatise maximal orders in a quaternion algebra ramified at $p$, being cited by [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.exists_isOrderCoord_of_isMaximalOrder`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.exists_isOrderCoord_of_isMaximalOrder) and by [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_idempotent_isSpecial_map_iff`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_idempotent_isSpecial_map_iff).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WittVector_exists_ringHom_padicInt_and_root_of_forall_sq_sub_mul_add_ne_zero.lean

